WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:06.399
Every morning, thousands of people all over the world begin their days with an invigorating session

2
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.518
of yoga, a form of exercise that involves stretching and breathing routines. Some of them chant

3
00:00:10.715 --> 00:00:15.009
while they work out; others listen to soothing music. Meanwhile, they improve their mental powers, tone

4
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:20.992
their muscles, and relax their busy minds. How does yoga accomplish this? While no one knows exactly

5
00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:23.325
how yoga is able to improve people’s physical, emotional, and spiritual states, many have benefited from

6
00:00:23.497 --> 00:00:31.876
it. Yoga, which has been practiced for thousands of years, is just one of many medical

7
00:00:31.977 --> 00:00:40.646
and health care systems that are collectively called alternative medicine&#8212;because they are different from conventional Western

8
00:00:40.877 --> 00:00:44.195
medicine. Most alternative medicines use natural methods and holistic approaches to healing, rather than the pharmaceuticals

9
00:00:44.922 --> 00:00:49.918
and surgery of conventional treatment. Alternative practitioners see illness as the result of an imbalance within

10
00:00:49.919 --> 00:00:54.011
the body. They believe that if people learn how to maintain balance in their lives, they

11
00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:59.216
will remain in good health indefinitely. Therefore, the goal of most alternative practitioners is to find the

12
00:00:59.318 --> 00:01:05.751
source of the imbalance&#8212;if one exists&#8212;and then treat it, as well as prevent it from happening

13
00:01:05.808 --> 00:01:11.861
again. Of course, each type of alternative medicine has its own way of accomplishing this. One

14
00:01:11.862 --> 00:01:17.074
ancient alternative medical system, dating back more than two thousand years, is traditional Chinese medicine (TCM).

15
00:01:17.075 --> 00:01:21.534
Its practitioners believe that a healthy body is a delicate balance between two opposing forces: yin

16
00:01:22.303 --> 00:01:30.319
and yang. The former represents the cold, passive functions, such as breathing, whereas the latter symbolizes

17
00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:37.366
the hot, active functions, such as digestion. Blood and chi (the life force or vital energy that

18
00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:46.795
keeps the body working properly) are believed to flow along 12 internal pathways called meridians. Illness

19
00:01:46.796 --> 00:01:56.456
is caused by an imbalance between yin and yang that blocks the flow of chi. TCM

20
00:01:56.457 --> 00:02:02.343
practitioners typically use a combination of massage and other therapies to unblock chi and restore balance

21
00:02:02.344 --> 00:02:10.971
to the body. Another of the methods TCM doctors use is acupuncture. This practice involves inserting

22
00:02:11.316 --> 00:02:14.944
small needles into the skin at one or more specific points along the patient’s meridians. The

23
00:02:15.209 --> 00:02:21.970
points, depending on their location, correspond to particular organs. For example, acupuncturists might carefully place a

24
00:02:22.454 --> 00:02:27.269
needle between the thumb and forefinger to treat a headache; or they might insert a needle into

25
00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:33.685
a specific spot on the leg to improve bowel function. Acupuncture is most often used to

26
00:02:33.889 --> 00:02:39.879
treat persistent pain&#8212;especially when conventional medical treatment has failed to do so. Even though thousands of

27
00:02:39.966 --> 00:02:46.851
people have turned to acupuncture, the concept of meridians is not based on scientific evidence. Scientists

28
00:02:47.807 --> 00:02:54.389
are just beginning to seriously study acupuncture, and they have not yet explained how the specific

29
00:02:54.602 --> 00:03:03.149
points might connect to internal organs. Many skeptics suggest that acupuncture works only because of the

30
00:03:03.333 --> 00:03:08.775
placebo effect. (A placebo is a dummy pill given to patients in scientific studies. The placebo

31
00:03:08.839 --> 00:03:13.261
effect, which has been scientifically documented, means that a person will show improvement simply because he or

32
00:03:13.479 --> 00:03:23.012
she believes a drug or treatment will work.) In other words, many scientists believe it is

33
00:03:23.107 --> 00:03:30.748
the patient’s expectation that makes acupuncture work, not the practice itself. One alternative therapy that has

34
00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:37.329
largely been accepted by the medical community is herbalism. This is the practice of drinking teas

35
00:03:37.401 --> 00:03:42.898
and other mixtures made from medicinal herbs and plants. An herbalist who is familiar with the

36
00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:51.741
properties of the ingredients carefully prepares each mixture and prescribes it to the patient. These mixtures

37
00:03:51.837 --> 00:03:58.003
might be drunk only once or many times, depending on the type of sickness. Some treatments are

38
00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:02.511
very complex mixtures of dozens of different herbs and plants. Others are as simple as herbal

39
00:04:02.825 --> 00:04:05.713
teas. Many people drink mint tea, for instance, before bed to aid digestion. Others might drink

40
00:04:05.769 --> 00:04:10.937
coffee or black tea (both herbal medicines although not always recognized as such) in the morning

41
00:04:10.938 --> 00:04:19.657
to boost their energy levels. Herbal remedies, unlike acupuncture, have been studied by scientists for many

42
00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:25.817
decades. In fact, numerous clinical trials have shown that many plants contain chemicals with medicinal properties,

43
00:04:25.966 --> 00:04:34.903
although often in very small amounts. Conventional pharmaceutical companies have even used herbal treatments as the

44
00:04:35.023 --> 00:04:41.300
basis for new drug research. For instance, aspirin, a medicine commonly used for pain relief and to

45
00:04:41.301 --> 00:04:46.591
reduce fevers, was originally derived from willow bark and used in teas and other drinks to

46
00:04:46.711 --> 00:04:55.266
calm nerves, relieve headaches, and reduce minor aches. Of course, aspirin is now completely synthetic, but

47
00:04:55.267 --> 00:05:02.611
its origin shows how scientists have learned from herbal remedies. Many doctors, however, still question whether

48
00:05:03.196 --> 00:05:13.304
alternative treatments can be fully integrated into conventional medicine because their results are often difficult to

49
00:05:14.016 --> 00:05:18.693
scientifically verify. Also, not all practitioners of alternative medicine have had formal training, nor are they

50
00:05:19.016 --> 00:05:25.025
required to belong to professional organizations, as medical doctors are. This means that patients are not

51
00:05:25.241 --> 00:05:31.943
guaranteed to receive the same quality of care from one alternative practitioner to the next. Advocates of

52
00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:36.191
alternative medicine are working hard to change this, and some have helped set up international regulatory

53
00:05:36.192 --> 00:05:43.886
boards to ensure that practitioners are well educated and offer high-quality care. However, these changes will

54
00:05:44.305 --> 00:05:47.608
take a long time. Practitioners of alternative medicine are hopeful, however, that their work will eventually

55
00:05:48.562 --> 00:05:57.114
be recognized as valid, and they have reason to be optimistic. Chiropractic, which developed in the

56
00:05:57.772 --> 00:06:07.271
early twentieth century, is an alternative medical practice that has achieved a high level of acceptance

57
00:06:07.801 --> 00:06:13.464
within the conventional health-care system. Chiropractors believe that each vertebra in the spine corresponds to an organ

58
00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:17.781
in the body, so when a vertebra is out of position, that organ is unhealthy. Their

59
00:06:17.782 --> 00:06:22.061
treatment involves adjusting the spine to correct any misalignments. Although there is still a fair amount

60
00:06:22.481 --> 00:06:26.373
of debate about the value of the treatment, there is ample evidence to suggest that chiropractors

61
00:06:26.561 --> 00:06:31.991
can reduce back pain and some headaches. As a result, many medical professionals encourage their patients

62
00:06:32.474 --> 00:06:40.811
with these problems to try chiropractic treatments in addition to regular medical care. The success of

63
00:06:41.797 --> 00:06:47.236
chiropractic medicine and the growing interest in practices such as yoga and herbalism have provided options

64
00:06:47.463 --> 00:06:53.063
for patients who have not had successful treatment from conventional doctors. In addition, TCM and other alternative

65
00:06:53.198 --> 00:06:59.941
medical systems provide preventive care for those who are healthy and want to stay that way.

66
00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:04.949
So, whether it is a morning session of yoga or a cup of hot herbal tea,

67
00:07:05.013 --> 00:07:11.063
many alternative medical methods are available to help people maintain good health and lead fulfilling lives.

